{
  "schemaVersion": "1.0",
  "scriptId": "td-05-speed-change-early-late-schedules",
  "sourceType": "MANUAL",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Changed Speed, Early/Late Arrival, and Schedules",
    "description": "Turn speed changes into time differences, solve early/late arrival equations, and recover the speed needed to meet a deadline.",
    "teachingApproach": "Begin with a fractional speed reduction so the inverse time effect is visible. Then use early-versus-late time differences to recover distance, build simple speed-change equations, handle delayed departures, and finish with remaining-distance deadline problems. Every schedule question is translated into distance, time used, and time left before arithmetic begins.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 30,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal, Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 18, Time and Distance. Approved scope: Cover late/early arrival from changed speed, distance from two speed-time conditions, speed increases that save fixed time, late departure with fixed arrival, percentage speed increases, two-condition speed/distance equations, and remaining-speed questions after part of a journey has already been completed."
  },
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn why a small speed change can make someone early or late.\n\nThe key is to keep the distance fixed. When speed changes, time changes in the opposite direction.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A trip normally takes T minutes. A traveller moves at only 4/5 of the usual speed.\n\nFor the same distance, time becomes 5/4 T.\nThe extra time is 1/4 T.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "If the traveller is 15 minutes late:\n\nT/4 = 15\nT = 60 minutes.\n\nWe found the usual time without needing the distance.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "q_1": {
